WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.254
Temperature sampling reshapes the data distribution
using a single exponent, tau.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.637
But there is a catch.

00:00:06.717 --> 00:00:10.523
When you tune tau to give the head languages more
presence,

00:00:10.603 --> 00:00:12.828
you end up over-repeating the tail.

00:00:12.908 --> 00:00:17.306
At tau equals three point three three, with a
trillion-token budget,

00:00:17.386 --> 00:00:21.850
the lowest-resource languages get repeated more
than a hundred times.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.328
That much repetition causes overfitting that hurts
downstream tasks,

00:00:26.408 --> 00:00:29.555
it raises the risk of memorizing private content,

00:00:29.635 --> 00:00:32.453
and it wastes compute on duplicate examples,

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:36.470
and every one of these harms only gets worse as
models scale.
